fact WorkItem(id: "WI-366", description: some(value: "WI-342 follow-up: fully retire make_denoted — migrate the ground-FACT value-in-type positions to value facts (gated on effect-expressions-as-types). After WI-342 T8 (commit 'WI-342 T8 wrap-up'), make_denoted is OFF the typer (T1-T7) and OFF every live value-in-type PRODUCTION path: entity fields (S4c), the Entity/EntityInfo schema facts (T8 'A'), op signatures (WI-348), and call type-args (T8 'C+B') all mint a Value::Node denoted via make_denoted_occ; a full-workspace probe confirms the loader no longer reaches make_denoted for any corpus input. make_denoted SURVIVES only as the GROUND (hash-consed) lowering in type_expr_to_term for the parameterized ground-FACT positions: SortAlias (sort-def 'sort T = ...'), SortView ('requires' / fact 'provides', via sort_inst_to_term + build_instantiation_term's Denoted placeholder at load.rs ~1085). (The redundant let k_type_name term slot was already dropped in T8 cleanup B.) These cannot carry a Value::Node until effect-expressions-as-types lets those fact slots THEMSELVES become value facts (a Modify[c] / value-in-type binding inside a SortView/SortAlias must ride as Value::Node, which a hash-consed TermId fact cannot hold). WORK: (1) make SortAlias / SortView / provides value facts — mirror the WI-348 OperationInfo + WI-342 EntityInfo/Entity value-fact split (build a Value head when any binding is Node, assert_fact_value, migrate consumers carrier-agnostically via rule_head_value/TermView); (2) THEN type_expr_to_term collapses to type_expr_to_value(ty).as_term().expect(ground) and make_denoted DELETES; rework the #[cfg(test)] cross-carrier fixtures (region.rs modify_label, mod.rs wi342 test, typing.rs cross-carrier tests) — keep a #[cfg(test)]-gated ground-denoted builder or raw alloc since the loader then emits only Node. CAUTION: the panicking as_term wrapper for type_expr_to_term was TRIED in T8 and REVERTED — /code-review empirically caught it regressing parseable programs that previously loaded as a ground denoted ('sort T = Vector[Int,3]', 'requires Vector[Int,3]'). So step (1) MUST precede the wrapper. Gated on effect-expressions-as-types (proposals 045/046 effect rows ride on the type representation; relates to WI-341 dependent arrows). Acceptance: ToolPasses(cargo-test); make_denoted deleted (or #[cfg(test)]-only); a SortAlias/SortView/provides value-in-type binding rides as Value::Node."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-390"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-06-14T20:11:45Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-366", author: "user", content: "WI-387 (delivered) concretely hit this WI's unfinished scope: the fact-vs-provides DIFFERENCE is 'term loses fact' (user). A 'fact Spec[...]' head lowers via the TERM path (convert_term) which is LOSSY -- a '{}'/effect-row binding value degrades to Term::Ref('{}') -> remap_symbol_strict -> UnresolvedName (the row is DROPPED), so a written effect row cannot ride on a fact head; a 'provides' clause lowers via the type-aware path (sort_inst_to_value -> type_expr_to_value/lower_effect_row) and KEEPS it. WI-387 ROUTED AROUND it (used 'provides Stream[T=T, E={}]' for List) and fixed the type-param-shape half: sort_inst_to_value now lowers a type-param binding to Ref(param) matching the fact-head convert_term shape, so the two emit the SAME dispatch wildcard (impl_param_ref only recognizes Ref/Ident, not the nullary Fn name_to_sort_term used to build -- that divergence broke wi210). The REMAINING difference is exactly this WI's step (1): make the fact-head / SortView / provides emission a VALUE FACT (build a Value::Node head when any binding is structured/denoted). PRINCIPLE (user): fact and provides must be NO different -- both declare ONE SortProvidesInfo capability; the term representation must not lose the fact. Finishing WI-366 (unify the fact-head term-path emission with the provides type-aware path -> byte-identical SortProvidesInfo) eliminates the difference; the WI-387 wi210/wi357 dispatch canaries must stay green either way. Sub-note: the EMPTY-row {} case is ground (lowers to a ground effects_rows term, not a Node), so it is a smaller convert-level recognition gap (term path must route a {} EffectRow TypeExpr to lower_effect_row instead of stringifying) that could land independently of the denoted-row Value::Node migration this WI is gated on (045/046 effect-expressions-as-types).", at: "2026-06-04T20:58:50Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-366", author: "user", content: "SCOPE ADD (user): migrate OperationInfo.requires and OperationInfo.ensures (op_info.rs OperationRecord, lines 61/64) from Vec<TermId> to Vec<Value> -- the LAST term-only fields on OperationInfo; params/return_type/effects already moved to Value (WI-341/348, 'read carrier-faithfully, never materialized to a term'). WHY: a denoted-bearing precondition (requires Modify[c] -- a value-in-type SortView) cannot ride as a hash-consed TermId, so the term-level readers SILENTLY SKIP the value-fact OperationInfo head (the 'let Some(head_named)=kb.fact_head_named_args(rid) else continue' pattern) -- a wi348-boundary-no-value-to-termid violation + 'term loses fact' at the requires/ensures level. Migrating to Value closes it. CAVEAT: requires/ensures are precondition/postcondition GOAL terms (WI-347), consumed by SLD-style goal handling (check_override_refinement filters the auto-inferred EffectsRuntime[Effects=E] requires; req_insertion::run; the resolver) -- so the struct-field change must land WITH carrier-agnostic (TermView) consumer reads, not alone (overlaps WI-348 consumer migration). SIBLING narrowing (migrate together for a uniform Value requires surface): the SORT-level RequiresEntry.spec is also TermId (typing.rs:10014), held in EnclosingSort.requires: Vec<RequiresEntry>. Part of B (the fact/requires value-in-type lossless migration) for the fresh WI-366 session.", at: "2026-06-04T21:36:24Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-366", author: "user", content: "make_denoted FULLY DELETED 2026-06-04 (commit 244aaa3, suite green). Was already #[cfg(test)] with ZERO production callers; probe confirmed no production/reflect path builds a ground denoted term (value-in-type is always Value::Node via make_denoted_occ; unify_denoted_view is carrier-agnostic and stays). Removed the method + 7 ground-vs-Node cross-carrier tests + ground_param (typing.rs); converted region.rs modify_label to a Node label (production-faithful); carved the dead TermId-twin out of the mod.rs wi342 arrow test (kept Value-form reads). Ground-denoted TermId carrier retired. REMAINING WI-366 scope is B only (fact-head value-fact + requires/ensures Vec<TermId>->Vec<Value>, recorded in prior feedback) -- for a fresh session.", at: "2026-06-04T21:55:41Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-366", author: "user", content: "SYNC + PIVOT 2026-06-05: rebased onto origin/main (which gained WI-087 + the remote's WI-389/HandlerAction). B1 DELIVERED (commit dbc8a7e, was 3389fdd): written effect-row {} rides the term path byte-identical to provides. B2a DELIVERED (commit f7b439b, was fb3026e): OperationInfo.requires/ensures -> Vec<Value> (op_info.rs merged with WI-087's new meta field; override tests green). B2b (RequiresEntry.spec -> Value) SUPERSEDED by new WI-390 (now a dependency of WI-366): attempting B2b hit the resolve_cache, keyed by (SortGoal, Vec<RequiresEntry>), which needs RequiresEntry: Hash+Eq -- and Value isn't Hash/Eq because a TermId is LOSSY for denoted, so a term-projection hash would be incorrect (user). That surfaced the real fork: option A (make Value a first-class key via structural_eq + a cached structural hash) vs option B (represent denoted FAITHFULLY in the Term world, admitting temporary/scoped term-store items). User chose B (WI-390): 'we can represent occurrence as term'; principle = prefer a single representation, but any second representation must be CORRECT (lossless), not a lossy projection. With WI-390, RequiresEntry.spec stays a faithful TermId, the cache stays TermId-keyed, and the carrier-split bug class dies -- so B2b's Value migration is dropped in favor of WI-390. WI-366's remaining 'carry denoted requires' goal now lands via WI-390.", at: "2026-06-05T05:58:45Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-366", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED 2026-06-14 (done-but-not-closed sweep; spot-verified GREEN). Dep WI-390 is Delivered (b474ef7/b183018) so not blocked. B1 (written effect-row {} rides the term path byte-identical to provides) — dbc8a7e, 4 tests in wi366_value_in_type_facts_test.rs. B2a (OperationInfo.requires/ensures -> Vec<Value>) — f7b439b, op_info.rs:65,69. B2b (RequiresEntry.spec->Value) superseded by WI-390 (Term world made lossless for denoted); *_rides_as_term tests pin a faithful hash-consed Term with the denoted value preserved. ACCEPTANCE CAVEAT: original said 'make_denoted deleted / #[cfg(test)]-only'; it was deleted (fa5d885) then WI-390 deliberately re-introduced a faithful form (mod.rs:3423) — the dependency overrode that sub-clause BY DESIGN, not a regression. Test module wired (wi_tests.rs:184). VERIFIED 2026-06-14: wi_tests -- wi366 = 14 passed / 0 failed. Tracking-only close.", at: "2026-06-14T20:11:41Z")
